# A branch in a scope called below nested list maps must retain its input dependency.

```catala
declaration enumeration Cabin:
  -- Basic
  -- Premium
  -- Business

declaration structure Journey:
  data cabin content Cabin
  data valid content integer
  data values content list of integer

declaration structure Charge:
  data amount content integer

declaration scope Tariff:
  input journey content Journey
  output amount content integer

scope Tariff:
  definition amount equals
    if [Premium; Business] contains journey.cabin then 0 else 1

declaration scope JourneyCost:
  input journey content Journey
  output charges content list of Charge

scope JourneyCost:
  assertion journey.valid = 42
  definition charges equals
    map each (left, right) among (journey.values, journey.values) to
      Charge { -- amount: (output of Tariff with { -- journey: journey }).amount
                         + left + right }

declaration scope NestedScopeMap:
  input journey content Journey
  output charges content list of list of Charge

scope NestedScopeMap:
  definition charges equals
    map each journey among [journey] to
      (output of JourneyCost with { -- journey: journey }).charges
```
